\subtree{
  \title{Exhaustiveness checking for arithmetic patterns in Disco}
  \p{I continued working on [this project from a couple weeks ago](00CG).  I made some progress with typechecking and desugaring of arithmetic patterns.  All that's left is to actually plug them into the exhaustiveness checker itself, and make it call out to the semilinear set solver appropriately... but after staring at it for a while, I realized I have no idea how the exhaustiveness checker works!  I suspect some refactoring will be needed, since there doesn't seem to be an obvious place to just stick in some extra code for arithmetic patterns.  Thankfully, the student who wrote it is still around; I hope we can meet about it soon and figure it out together.}
